; Deliberately empty of settings. Read this before adding one.
;
; Do NOT add `legacy-peer-deps=true`. It makes npm ignore peerDependencies
; entirely — a conflicting peer produces no warning, and `--strict-peer-deps`
; does not override it. `@antiphony/shared` declares `zod` as a peer so that a
; consumer's npm enforces a single shared zod instance; this repo needs to see
; that kind of conflict in its own tree too. The tree resolves its peers cleanly
; without it.
;
; Peer checking does not catch an upstream peer range that is simply wrong
; (#148: `@hono/zod-openapi` declared `zod: >=3.0.0` but needed zod 3), so it is
; a floor, not a guarantee.
;
; If you hit a peer conflict you cannot resolve, use `overrides` in the root
; package.json for that ONE package: narrow, visible in a diff, and it does not
; switch off peer resolution for the whole tree.
